atom     signatures/capture-parameter-order
source   curated
kind     parse grid — compiled with -c, never run

# A capture parameter takes everything that is left, so a REQUIRED parameter
# after it could never be filled. Rakudo rejects such a signature at compile
# time — "Cannot put required parameter ... after variadic parameters" — for
# both the `$b` and the `\b` form. rakupp accepts both. A NAMED parameter after
# a capture is legal, and so is a raw sigil BEFORE one, which is why those
# neighbours are here: they bound the divergence.
#
# Recorded from files written byte-exactly and compiled with -c. Two earlier
# readings of this atom were wrong — one taken from an EVAL probe, one from a
# file written with `echo`, which turned the `\b` into a backspace and compiled
# a different program. The lesson is the atom's own: an observation must be
# captured the way the test will reproduce it.

- id     0001
  from   review:2026-08-18 · a positional after a capture can never be filled
  code   sub f(|c, $b) { 1 }
  no-parse yes
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → rejected: Cannot put required parameter $b after variadic parameters
  oracle rakupp-v3.14.0-107-gb8ea9bb-modified → compiles

- id     0002
  from   review:2026-08-18 · the raw-sigil form is rejected for the same reason
  code   sub f(|c, \b) { 1 }
  no-parse yes
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → rejected: Cannot put required parameter b after variadic parameters
  oracle rakupp-v3.14.0-107-gb8ea9bb-modified → compiles

- id     0003
  from   review:2026-08-18 · a named after a capture is legal
  code   sub f(|c, :$b) { 1 }
  parses yes
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → compiles
  oracle rakupp-v3.14.0-107-gb8ea9bb-modified → compiles

- id     0004
  from   review:2026-08-18 · the ordinary form
  code   sub f($a, |c) { 1 }
  parses yes
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → compiles
  oracle rakupp-v3.14.0-107-gb8ea9bb-modified → compiles

- id     0005
  from   review:2026-08-18 · a capture alone
  code   sub f(|c) { 1 }
  parses yes
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → compiles
  oracle rakupp-v3.14.0-107-gb8ea9bb-modified → compiles

- id     0006
  from   review:2026-08-18 · a raw sigil BEFORE a capture is fine on both
  code   sub f(\a, |c) { 1 }
  parses yes
  oracle rakudo-2026.07 → compiles
  oracle rakupp-v3.14.0-107-gb8ea9bb-modified → compiles
